<div type="commentary">
      	<p>
      		See <bibl><ptr target="bib:ARIE1937-1938"/></bibl> (p. 87, §23) notes:<note>Text standardised according to DHARMA transliteration scheme.</note>
		<quote>No. 468 dated in the 13th
			year of an unspecified king, but which paleographically resembles the record of
			Nandivarman noticed above [DHARMA_INSPallava00325<!--EF update-->], may be assigned to the same king. This inscription
			gives the name of the god of Maṇalūr as Tiru-Uḻutīśvarattu Mahādeva, <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi>,
			Mahādeva of Uḷutīśvaram (Rudreśvaram?), but the origin of this name is not clear.</quote>
	</p>	
